Our work is focused on assisting users in exploration of spatially referenced data, i.e., economical,&#13;
demographic, ecological, etc. data referring to geographical objects or locations. Analysis such is&#13;
impossible without representing them maps. The main weakness Geographic Information Systems&#13;
(GISes) support mapping that the user not given any guidance designing presentations&#13;
whereas improper selection visualization methods can impede subsequent analysis even result in&#13;
wrong conclusions. Correct map design requires special knowledge from field thematic&#13;
cartography. One cannot presume GIS has this knowledge.&#13;
We introduce software system IRIS incorporates form of&#13;
generic, domain-independent rules. On basis it automatically generates thematic maps properly&#13;
presenting user’s data. Another distinctive feature supports with&#13;
the use generated interactively manipulate presentations, and response they&#13;
dynamically change making more salient various features under analysis.
